msgid "Update"
msgstr ""

msgid "We're pleased to announce the release of Quarkus 3.38."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As most of the development effort for new features and major upgrades is now "
"focused on Quarkus 4, this release is lighter on features than usual.\n"
"It still comes with the following notable features:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pull/55284[#55284] - Support weight-"
"based eviction for Hibernate 2LC Caffeine cache regions"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus HTTP Problem added to the Platform"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To update to Quarkus 3.38, we recommend updating to the latest version of "
"the Quarkus CLI and run:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that `quarkus update` can update your applications from any version of "
"Quarkus (including 2.x) to Quarkus 3.38."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For more information about the adjustments you need to make to your "
"applications, please refer to the https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/"
"Migration-Guide-3.38[Quarkus 3.38 migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Weight-based eviction for Hibernate second level Caffeine cache regions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 3.38 introduces support for weight-based (memory) eviction for "
"Hibernate second level cache Caffeine cache regions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Previously, only count-based eviction was available, meaning you could only "
"configure the maximum number of entries per cache region.\n"
"With weight-based eviction, you can now configure eviction based on the "
"estimated memory footprint of cached entities, providing more precise "
"control over cache memory usage."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus Platform"
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus HTTP Problem"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://github.com/quarkiverse/quarkus-http-problem[Quarkus HTTP Problem] "
"has been added to the Quarkus Platform."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This extension implements the https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457[RFC "
"9457] (Problem Details for HTTP APIs) standard, automatically mapping "
"exceptions to standardized `application/problem+json` HTTP responses."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It provides built-in exception mappers for common exceptions, prevents "
"leaking stack traces and implementation details, and integrates with OpenAPI "
"for auto-generated error documentation."
msgstr ""

